ghpull:790 a bl:PullRequest, bl:WorkItem ;
    rdfs:label "sparql_endpoint: bump store.generation after GSP DELETE's reasoner delta" ;
    bl:number 790 ;
    bl:state bl:Open ;
    bl:closesIssue ghissues:781 .

session:claudeSonnet5 a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "Claude Sonnet 5" .

session:pr790 a agp:AgentSession ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    prov:used ghissues:781 ;
    prov:startedAtTime "2026-11-11T17:42:07Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-11-11T17:42:07Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

session:pr790Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #781 is one of several follow-ups filed from PR #774's investigation of #591 (deletions not propagating to inferred facts): #774 fixed sparql_update.rs's CLEAR/DROP handlers, which called apply_reasoner_delta (mutating quads directly via QuadTable, bypassing Datastore's generation-incrementing wrapper methods) without a trailing store.generation += 1, defeating If-Match ETag preconditions and transaction optimistic-concurrency checks. #781 asked whether the SPARQL 1.1 Graph Store HTTP Protocol's DELETE route (gsp_delete_inner in graph_store.rs) had the same gap, since it calls the same apply_reasoner_delta path when a reasoner is configured." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:790 ;
    agp:decisionPoint session:pr790Decision ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr790 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .

session:pr790Decision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "Confirmed gsp_delete_inner had the exact same gap by first reproducing it: wrote a test driving the mutation through DELETE /{name}/data?graph=<g> (mirroring #774's clear_graph_reasoner_desync.rs test) and verified it reproduced the reported symptom — a stale If-Match ETag wrongly accepted with 200 instead of a 412 rejection — against the unfixed code, before adding the one-line fix (store.generation += 1; after the reasoner branch's apply_reasoner_delta call), mirroring #774's fix verbatim rather than inventing a different pattern." ;
    agp:alternative "Considered pushing the generation bump down into apply_reasoner_delta itself (or its apply_deletions/apply_insertions callees) so no caller could forget it again — rejected for this PR as a larger refactor than #781's stated scope, and because #774 already established the per-call-site pattern; a follow-up to centralize the bump is worth its own issue if a third call site turns up." .
